WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.820
Use timing to distinguish these repair processes.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.777
During copying, DNA polymerase can catch a wrong base it

00:00:07.777 --> 00:00:12.835
just added. Its exonuclease activity removes that incorrect base from

00:00:12.835 --> 00:00:14.114
the three prime end.

00:00:15.142 --> 00:00:19.710
After replication is complete, mismatch repair proteins scan the new

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.890
double helix. When they find a mismatch,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.532
enzymes remove the affected section and replace it with the

00:00:26.532 --> 00:00:28.479
correct DNA nucleotides.

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:34.113
Proofreading is a check during copying by DNA polymerase itself.

00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:37.399
Mismatch repair is a check after replication.

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:41.463
Both correct mistakes, but the timing and the proteins doing

00:00:41.463 --> 00:00:44.110
the checking distinguish the two processes.
